course: dictionary
lesson: 6659
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, show you which meaning the writer means. «Seesaws, scissors, wheelbarrows, bottle openers, nutcrackers, tongs and even your own arm are all levers.» The list is of tools and machines, so a nutcracker here is a tool.
explain: «Jays and nutcrackers hide thousands of nuts in autumn and remember most of the places months later.» Jays hide nuts, so a nutcracker here is a bird, not a tool. Always ask: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence. «A nutcracker squeezes hardest on a nut placed close to the hinge.» Squeezing a nut against a hinge only makes sense for the tool, so this nutcracker is the tool.
fact: A nutcracker is a tool for cracking the hard shells of nuts.
fact: A nutcracker can also be a wooden doll shaped like a soldier, popular at Christmas.
fact: «The Nutcracker» is a famous Christmas ballet with music by Tchaikovsky.
fact: A nutcracker can also be a bird of the crow family that eats nuts and seeds.
fact: In science, a nutcracker is a simple machine: a lever.
exercise: «Seesaws, scissors, wheelbarrows, bottle openers, nutcrackers, tongs and even your own arm are all levers.» In this sentence, what is a nutcracker? | *A simple tool, a lever | A Christmas ballet | A bird that eats seeds | A wooden soldier doll
exercise: «Jays and nutcrackers hide thousands of nuts in autumn.» What is a nutcracker in this sentence? | A tool for cracking shells | A famous ballet | A soldier doll | *A bird of the crow family
exercise: What is «The Nutcracker»? | A bird that hides food | *A famous Christmas ballet with music by Tchaikovsky | A dance on ice | A kind of nut
test: «A nutcracker squeezes hardest on a nut placed close to the hinge.» Which meaning fits best? | A doll shaped like a soldier | A Christmas ballet | *A tool for cracking nuts | A bird that hides nuts
test: A wooden doll shaped like a soldier is which meaning of nutcracker? | *A doll | A bird | A tool | A ballet
exam: «Jays and nutcrackers hide thousands of nuts in autumn and remember most of the places months later.» Which meaning fits best? | *A bird of the crow family that eats nuts | A Christmas ballet | A soldier doll | A tool for cracking shells
